class Solution {
    public List<Boolean> kidsWithCandies(int[] candies, int extraCandies) {
        List<Boolean> result = new ArrayList<>();
        
        // Step 1: Find the maximum candies among all kids
        int max = 1; //since min is 1, in constaint
        for (int candy : candies) {
            max = Math.max(max, candy);
        }
        
        // Step 2: Check each kid
        for (int candy : candies) {
            result.add(candy + extraCandies >= max);
        }
        
        return result;
    }
}



//Always initialize your maximum tracking variable to either the first element of the array or Integer.MIN_VALUE for edge cases

Time Complexity: O(n) You loop through the candies array exactly twice (once to find the max, once to build the result). 
Space Complexity: O(1) The only extra space used is for the result list 
